<title>USA: Goldman Sachs to buy Stockton asset management.</title>
<headline>Goldman Sachs to buy Stockton asset management.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Goldman Sachs Asset Management, the global investment management unit of Goldman, Sachs &amp; Co, said it agreed to acquire Commodities Corp Ltd, the asset management subsidiary of Stockton Holdings Ltd.</p>
<p>As part of the deal, Goldman Sachs said it will provide Stockton the investment services historically provided by Commodities, and Goldman Sachs will make an equity investment in Stockton.</p>
<p>Terms were not disclosed.  Both Goldman Sachs and Stockton are privately-held.  (c) Reuters Limited 1997</p>
